Error: Jet.RejectOutsideTemplate: `reject` runs only inside a marker's `expand` template or `check` rule.
  --> Tests/UI/MarkerDeclarations/reject_outside_a_marker_template.jet:11:13
    |
 11 | run: fn() { reject(Oops{}) }
    |             ^^^^^^
 Why: `reject(value)` raises a diagnostic at a marker's use site while the compiler expands the marker, or at a call its `check` rule hears; ordinary code has no use site to report at, so the call has nothing to run.
 Fix: Move the check into a marker's `expand: fn(self, target: Target)` or `check: fn(self, call: CompilerCall)` body, or return an error value from this function instead.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.RejectOutsideTemplate
